00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.520
Timely order processing
is key to any business.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.990
But it frequently involves
various systems, manual steps,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.700
and waiting for approvals.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.220
AppSheet automation
helps solve THIS

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.720
by enabling anyone on the team
to quickly and intelligently

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.710
automate a process.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.350
Let's look at the platform.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.290
The [INAUDIBLE] platform
anticipates your automation

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.500
requirements, provides
intelligent suggestions,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.430
and auto-constructs actions,
based on user intent.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:47.610
It's super easy to
create a new automation.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.460
Process steps can be
described in plain English,

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.700
starting to type "approval"
prompts contextual suggestions.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.500
Steps can be quickly added to
monitor your business process,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.430
and details can be added
later, or picked for you.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.340
Let's fast forward to the
last step in the process.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.690
Let's add a final step to send
the invoice to the customer.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.090
The platform already
generates the invoice,

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.570
highlights possible
recipients, and even

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:17.400
auto-fills relevant
details for you.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.540
Great, we are done
building our process.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.270
Now, let's see this
automation in action.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.980
As a new order gets
added in Salesforce,

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.690
our process is triggered.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.930
Since it's a high
value order, it's

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:32.560
